// ===========================================================================
// ⭐ THE CANONICAL TARGET for the ServiceRequest membership chain (#189).
//
// The acceptance criterion (operator, 2026-08-30):
//
//     an SR whose code IS in the value set          -> true  -> Approve
//     an SR whose code is NOT in it, nothing newer  -> false -> Deny
//     no SR at all, OR the SR carries no code       -> unanswered: pause and ask
//
// ⭐ THE WHOLE POINT: rows 2 and 3 are DIFFERENT. A request for some other
// service is a determinate NO — the request was read and it is not covered. No
// request at all is a question nobody has answered. Collapsing them is the
// defect this fixture exists to prevent.
//
// ⭐⭐ WHAT "NOT IN THE VALUE SET" MEANS IN ROW 2 — RULED (operator, 2026-09-02),
// because it was misread once and cost a planning round.
//
// "it" is the COVERED set, NOT the retrieve set. Row 2 says: *we adjudicate this
// kind of request, and this particular one is not covered.*
//
// A ServiceRequest for something this policy was never asked about — a
// colonoscopy, under a blepharoplasty policy — is NOT a missed row 2. It is not
// an instance of the concept at all, so it never reaches the predicate and the
// determination stays unestablished. Denying it would be a WRONG answer wearing
// a confident face; pausing says "this policy has nothing to say here".
//
// ⚠ THEREFORE `coded from` IS NOT AN OPTIMIZATION. It states what the concept is
// ABOUT — which requests are candidate answers — and that is what makes
// `most recent this` MEANINGFUL. Drop it and every ServiceRequest in the record
// competes: a routine lab order dated later than the RFA request wins the
// recency race and denies the RFA. A retrieve scoped by nothing ranks by nothing.
//
// ⚠⚠ THE TWO ALTERNATIVES WERE WORKED THROUGH AND REJECTED. Recorded so they are
// not re-proposed — both failures are structural, not tunable:
//
//   (1) NO `coded from` — an unfiltered retrieve. Every ServiceRequest competes;
//       a later unrelated order wins recency and DENIES. This trades a
//       recoverable pause for a confident WRONG answer, which is worse in kind.
//
//   (2) ONE set doing both jobs. Every record surviving a filter for set X is a
//       member of X, so the predicate can never return false. Row 2 disappears
//       BY IDENTITY.
//
// ⭐⭐ THE SHAPE: A CODED SUBJECT + AN EPHEMERAL PREDICATE.
//
// The question a human is asked is WHICH SERVICE was requested — a coded
// dropdown whose options are the requestable universe. Coverage is then COMPUTED
// from that answer, not asked separately.
//
// ⚠ The predicate is NOT directly assertable, and a `code is` beside it is a
// validator ERROR (charter §3 exception, operator 2026-09-02). Coverage is a
// FUNCTION of the requested service, not an independent clinical fact: a local
// answer would be a second source of truth for something derived, and the
// recency merge would arbitrate between an ANSWER and its own COMPUTATION.
// Overriding the conclusion is expressed by answering the SUBJECT differently.
//
// ⚠ BOTH terminologies are INSTANTIATED, and that is required rather than
// stylistic: membership is MECHANICAL (against the emitted set, never a resolved
// expansion), so two PURE REFERENCE sets each emit a DIFFERENT single-code stub
// and no datum could ever be in both — the approve row would vanish by identity,
// the mirror of failure (2) above.
// ===========================================================================
library "Endoluminal Ablation Coverage".

// What a user may be asked to pick, and what this concept is ABOUT.
terminology "Requestable Services":
- system is `http://www.ama-assn.org/go/cpt`.
// `37718` is endoluminal RFA (the covered one); `37722` is a fem-pop bypass — requestable, NOT covered.
- code is `37718`.
- code is `37722`.

// What this policy pays for. ⚠ A DIFFERENT set: see failure (2) above.
terminology "Covered Services":
- system is `http://www.ama-assn.org/go/cpt`.
- code is `37718`.

// THE QUESTION. Its arms are the local `code is` (a clinician answers the
// dropdown directly) and the ServiceRequest the policy reads. `most recent this`
// merges them, so a newer assertion overrides an older record and vice versa.
concept "Requested Service":
- shape is Record.
- type is Observation.
- value type is CodeableConcept.
- value from "Requestable Services".
- code is `requested-service`.
- definition is most recent this.
- source representation:
  - type is ServiceRequest.
  - coded from "Requestable Services".

// THE DETERMINATION — computed, never asserted. Three states: the requested
// service is covered / is not covered / has not been established at all.
concept "Requested Service Is Covered":
- shape is Scalar.
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- definition is "Requested Service" in "Covered Services".

activity "Approve Endoluminal Ablation":
- request CPGCommunicationRequest.
- with `APPROVED`.

activity "Deny Endoluminal Ablation":
- request CPGCommunicationRequest.
- with `NOT APPROVED`.

// If coverage cannot be established from the data, the tree PAUSES and the
// questionnaire asks which service was requested — that is the point of the chain.
decision "Endoluminal Ablation Coverage":
first:
- when "Requested Service Is Covered" then recommend activity "Approve Endoluminal Ablation".
- otherwise then recommend activity "Deny Endoluminal Ablation".
